appendix(14,True)
p('The team reviewed 358 unique selected app-review IDs across 21 app, storefront and language cohorts. The first wave contains 210 records from Google Play and the Apple App Store. The extension adds 148 distinct Google Play records across nine listing views. The date comparison below uses the 50 original Digiroom records only.')
picture('app_reviews','Figure A14.1. Review publication relative to Digiroom’s relaunch. A specific interaction can describe a failed attempt as well as a successful one.')
table(['Digiroom review test','Observed result','Interpretation'],[
 ['Favorable ratings in original Indonesian-language Play Store view','16/20 had four or five stars','Star rating alone gives no app-task or transaction outcome.'],
 ['What the 16 favorable reviews described','7 specific app interactions; 5 unclear; 4 other experiences or no experienced job','If every unclear record is counted as an interaction, the range is 7/16–12/16. It is a coding range.'],
 ['Usefulness of relaunch date','37 records before the date and 13 on or after it; 6 of the latter describe a specific app interaction','Publication date gives period context. It does not identify the build a reviewer used.'],
 ['Selection check across nine matched apps','Indonesian and English listing selections showed zero overlap in displayed review IDs','Separate storefront and language views. Avoid ranking apps using their selected reviews.'],
 ],[5.6,5.35,6.05])
a=p('Sources: selected public Google Play and Apple App Store listings, team review of date, task and rating, and the relaunch date in IBSC (2026, p. 4). ');hlink(a,'Digiroom on Google Play',url='https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=id.co.astra.ai.dev1&hl=id&gl=ID')

appendix(15,True)
p('The X collection covers ten exports from 1 January 2025 to 13 November 2026. Deduplication reduced 14,892 rows to 14,291 platform IDs. Of 6,186 replies, 5,704 lack the immediate parent in the export. All 37 captured post bodies explicitly naming Digiroom came from Auto2000’s named account. The collection is more useful for individual ownership choices than for measuring app usage.')
table(['Paraphrased account','Specific action or decision','Implication for KEY'],[
 ['Test-drive inquiry','Prospective buyer reported wanting to buy and being unable to find a test-drive unit.','A drive request needs a model, a confirmed vehicle and a named adviser.'],
 ['Older Toyota restoration','Owner reported a Rp100m purchase and Rp25m in combined suspension work and audio upgrades, comparing it with a younger used car around Rp120m.','Repair and immediate replacement can be competing outcomes for the same household. The amount bundles several costs.'],
 ['Choosing a workshop by job','One poster separates routine servicing, body repairs, parts and specialist work. Another describes a community workshop referral during a breakdown.','An owner may already know where to go. The offer has to earn the specific job.'],
 ['Sole-car household','A poster admired competing technology and described keeping a Japanese option while supporting only one car.','The family’s backup options can change what it needs to learn on a drive.'],
 ],[4.0,7.05,5.95])
a=p('Source: targeted retrieval and manual reading of selected X accounts. The examples describe reported choices. ');hlink(a,'Test-drive post',url='https://x.com/i/web/status/2003711716526563346');a.add_run('  |  ');hlink(a,'Restoration post',url='https://x.com/i/web/status/1988319241666441699')

appendix(16,True)
p('The three returned video threads contain 74 comment records. The Neta resale thread supplies 45. Video subject, audience and replies shape what is discussed, so the excerpts are used to compare mechanisms.')
picture('yt','Figure A16.1. A single video accounts for 45 of 74 comment records.')
table(['Observed theme','Paraphrased example','Implication'],[
 ['Charging access','One commenter reported relying on public charging rather than installing the supplied wall charger. Replies disputed installation-cost details.','Ask where the household can actually charge and what it does when that option is unavailable.'],
 ['Service recovery','One BYD M6 commenter described a window-noise remedy at a named outlet.','An account of a completed remedy illustrates the value of a named endpoint and closure.'],
 ['Resale and support','A Neta discussion raised dealer continuity as a rival explanation for resale concern.','Separate resale prices, battery condition, and continued dealer or parts support.'],
 ],[4.0,7.0,6.0])
